<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Emboabas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1707–1709</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Emboabas was a conflict in the gold fields of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minas-gerais">Minas Gerais</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, between the Paulistas who had discovered the gold and the newcomers from Portugal and other parts of Brazil, called emboabas. The newcomers, led by Manuel Nunes Viana, drove the Paulistas from the main mining districts. The crown responded by creating the Captaincy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-paulo">São Paulo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meena">Minas</a> de Ouro in 1709.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-emboabas.jpg" alt="War of the Emboabas" width="320" height="268" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guerra_dos_Emboabas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
